 Add `--json` to get a JSON object instead.
 
+### Caching
+
+Parsing dominates the runtime on large files. Pass `--cache` to store the
+parsed records on disk and reuse them on the next run over the same file:
+
+```
+logslice --cache huge.log --count-by level   # parses and caches
+logslice --cache huge.log --level error      # served from the cache
+```
+
+Cached results are stored as JSON, one entry per log file, in the first of:
+`$LOGSLICE_CACHE_DIR` (used as-is), `$XDG_CACHE_HOME/logslice`, or
+`~/.cache/logslice`. The cache key includes the file's size and modification
+time, so editing or appending to a log invalidates its entry. Entries expire
+after one hour by default; pass `--cache-ttl SECONDS` to change the TTL.
+Delete the cache directory to clear the cache.
+
 ## Development
 
 ```
